        "Your mission is to defeat the final boss, the puzzle of power in close relationships: hold dyadic power theory up to the light and see why equal-power couples display more dominance cues than unequal ones, why the powerful have less need to demonstrate their power, why the chilling effect silences the less powerful partner, and why low-power men explode with aggressiveness when their situational power also fails; then walk the subordination hypothesis and the finding that women in equal-power heterosexual relationships use more dominant cues than their male partners; finish against the cost of dominance, the intimidation strategies that backfire, the staring that kills helping, and the skilled balance between friendliness and dominance that makes influence endure.",
